    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0706" n="614" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 800.6354/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of the Japanese Embassy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Tanaka</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Foreign Trade Adviser of the
                        Department of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 28, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received October 25.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Lay</hi>: The matter of joining the inter-Allied tin committee,
                    which formed a part of our conversation on the 18th instant, has been duly taken
                    up with my Government who now inform us that a telegraphic instruction was
                    despatched on the 7th of September detailing a member of the Japanese Embassy at
                    London to take part on that committee representing the Japanese Government.</p>
                <p>Yours very truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">T. Tanaka</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
